{"repositoryId":1222364952,"availability":"available","full":"gilgamish-hub/legal-auditor-ai","name":"legal-auditor-ai","description":"Contract clause classifier: fine-tuned LegalBERT on CUAD, 88.4% accuracy on unseen contracts. Streamlit app with risk flags, explanations and PDF reports.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-04-27T09:43:39Z","updated":"2026-10-13T20:25:56Z","license":null,"branch":"main","homepage":"https://jatin-legal-auditor.streamlit.app","topics":["bert","huggingface","legal-tech","machine-learning","nlp","pytorch","streamlit","text-classification","transformers"],"demo":"https://jatin-legal-auditor.streamlit.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-16T02:47:44.981Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-16T02:47:44.981Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-16T02:47:44.981Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-16T02:47:44.981Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Legal Auditor AI takes a contract (pasted text or a PDF), splits it into clauses and classifies each clause with a fine-tuned LegalBERT model into one of 19 clause types (Governing Law, Limitation of Liability, Anti-Assignment, Audit Rights, ...) or Other. Each clause gets a risk level and the words that influenced the prediction most.","It then asks the opposite question: which clause types should be in this contract and are not? A distribution agreement with no Limitation of Liability and no Audit Rights is unusual, and that is a finding no per-clause label can express. \"Unusual\" is measured, not assumed — against the base rates of the 510 annotated contracts, within the same contract type where there is enough data for one.","The labels come from CUAD, a public dataset of 510 commercial contracts annotated by lawyers."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/gilgamish-hub/legal-auditor-ai/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f8b1ad87df7e0644bd525206fae0e15ad65748e7d13add6215c